You are a Principal Full-Stack Engineer, AI Systems Architect, Security Engineer, and Senior UI/UX Designer.

Your task is to evolve the existing Nexus AI project into a premium, production-ready AI productivity platform while preserving every working feature.

## CORE OBJECTIVES

Do NOT rebuild the project from scratch.

Instead:

- Preserve the existing architecture.
- Preserve all Gemini API functionality.
- Preserve authentication.
- Preserve chat functionality.
- Preserve responsiveness.
- Preserve routing.
- Improve the application with clean, modular, scalable production-quality code.

Avoid duplicate code.

Follow modern software engineering best practices.

--------------------------------------------
1. AUTHENTICATION IMPROVEMENTS
--------------------------------------------

Simplify the login experience.

The Login page should contain ONLY:

• Username or Email
• Password

The first field must accept either:

- Username
OR
- Email

The backend should automatically determine which one was entered and authenticate using the same endpoint.

Keep:

• Remember Me
• Forgot Password
• Create Account

Do NOT modify the registration process.

Registration should continue collecting:

- Full Name
- Username
- Email
- Password
- Existing required fields

Maintain:

- Session persistence
- Secure authentication
- Protected routes
- Existing AI functionality

--------------------------------------------
2. AI WORKSPACES
--------------------------------------------

Replace the generic AI experience with intelligent workspaces.

There should NOT be a popup saying:

"Select Workspace"

or

"Choose Workspace"

Instead, permanently display all workspaces inside the application navigation.

Desktop:
Left Sidebar

Tablet:
Navigation Drawer

Mobile:
Navigation Drawer or Bottom Navigation

Available Workspaces

🧠 General AI

💻 Coding Assistant

📚 Study Assistant

💼 Business Assistant

✍️ Writing Assistant

🔬 Research Assistant

📊 Data Analysis Assistant

🎨 Creative Assistant

🌍 Translation Assistant

--------------------------------------------
3. WORKSPACE EXPERIENCE
--------------------------------------------

Each workspace should have:

• Professional icon

• Name

• Short overview

• Dedicated hidden system prompt

• Suggested starter prompts

• Independent conversation history

• Unique personality

• Shared chat interface

Clicking a workspace should:

• Instantly activate it

• Highlight it

• Switch AI behaviour

• Keep the same page

• Never reload

• Never ask for confirmation

• Remember the last workspace

• Restore it automatically after login

--------------------------------------------
4. SYSTEM PROMPTS
--------------------------------------------

Every workspace should use its own internal system prompt.

The system prompt MUST NEVER be visible to users.

Users must NOT be able to:

• View it

• Copy it

• Export it

• Inspect it

• Retrieve it

Instead, show a short overview describing what that workspace can do.

Example:

Coding Assistant

"Write, explain, debug and optimize software across multiple programming languages."

Business Assistant

"Generate business plans, marketing strategies, SWOT analyses and professional business documents."

Study Assistant

"Create lesson notes, quizzes, flashcards and revision plans."

When a workspace is selected:

Automatically prepend the hidden system prompt before every Gemini request.

The user should never notice this process.

--------------------------------------------
5. CHAT EXPERIENCE
--------------------------------------------

Preserve every existing feature.

Improve where necessary.

Support:

✓ Markdown

✓ Syntax highlighting

✓ Streaming responses (when available)

✓ Regenerate

✓ Stop Generation

✓ Multiple conversations

✓ Search conversations

✓ Rename conversations

✓ Delete conversations

✓ Export conversations

--------------------------------------------
6. COPY BUTTON
--------------------------------------------

Replace every text button saying:

"Copy"

with a professional icon.

Preferred icons:

- Lucide Copy

- Material Design content_copy

- Font Awesome fa-copy

When pressed:

1. Copy the response

2. Animate smoothly

3. Replace the icon with a green checkmark

4. Return to the copy icon after approximately two seconds

Desktop:

Show tooltip:

Copy

Mobile:

No tooltip.

Ensure accessibility and touch-friendly sizing.

--------------------------------------------
7. RESPONSIVE DESIGN
--------------------------------------------

The entire application must work perfectly on:

✓ Phones

✓ Tablets

✓ Laptops

✓ Desktop Monitors

Requirements:

No overlapping UI

No horizontal scrolling

Responsive typography

Flexible layouts

Touch-friendly controls

Consistent spacing

Dark Mode support

Light Mode support

--------------------------------------------
8. CODE ARCHITECTURE
--------------------------------------------

Organize the project cleanly.

Separate:

Authentication

Routes

Workspace Configuration

Workspace Prompts

Components

Pages

Utilities

API Services

Styles

Icons

Settings

Future workspaces should be easy to add.

--------------------------------------------
9. PERFORMANCE
--------------------------------------------

Optimize for:

Fast startup

Minimal bundle size

Lazy loading where appropriate

Smooth animations

Efficient rendering

Clean state management

Production-quality code

--------------------------------------------
10. QUALITY ASSURANCE
--------------------------------------------

Before completion verify:

✓ Username login works

✓ Email login works

✓ Registration works

✓ Logout works

✓ Session persistence works

✓ Protected routes work

✓ Gemini API works

✓ AI chat works

✓ Workspace switching works

✓ Hidden system prompts work

✓ Separate histories work

✓ Copy icon works

✓ No console errors

✓ No routing errors

✓ No broken links

✓ No server errors

✓ Fully responsive

--------------------------------------------
11. IMPLEMENTATION REPORT
--------------------------------------------

After implementation provide:

1. Files created

2. Files modifimaa
Deliver a complete, polished, production-ready implementation with no placeholder code, TODOs, or unfinished features.